# Think Before Coding

- State assumptions explicitly before implementation.
- If requirements are ambiguous, present interpretations instead of silently choosing one.
- If multiple reasonable interpretations exist, ask for clarification before coding.
- If a simpler approach exists, call it out; push back on unnecessary complexity.
- Research existing in-repo patterns, helpers, commands, and tests before adding new architecture.
- If something is unclear, stop and ask a clarifying question.
